From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: wine.inf: pass parameters through the .msi verbs

HKCR\Msi.Package\shell\Open (and Repair, Uninstall) was "msiexec /i "%1"",
so ShellExecute of a .msi dropped the caller's parameters. winget launches MSI
installers that way with /passive /norestart /log; msiexec started with full
interactive UI instead and waited for a click that never came -- every
winget MSI install hung. Windows' command ends in %*, as these now do.

The values are also written on update (no FLG_ADDREG_NOCLOBBER), so existing
prefixes are repaired by the next wineboot -u, not only new ones.

--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -314,9 +314,9 @@
 HKCR,MediaFoundation,,16
 HKCR,Msi.Package,,2,"Windows Installer Package"
 HKCR,Msi.Package\DefaultIcon,,2,"msiexec.exe"
-HKCR,Msi.Package\shell\Open\command,,2,"%11%\msiexec.exe /i ""%1"""
-HKCR,Msi.Package\shell\Repair\command,,2,"%11%\msiexec.exe /f ""%1"""
-HKCR,Msi.Package\shell\Uninstall\command,,2,"%11%\msiexec.exe /x ""%1"""
+HKCR,Msi.Package\shell\Open\command,,,"%11%\msiexec.exe /i ""%1"" %*"
+HKCR,Msi.Package\shell\Repair\command,,,"%11%\msiexec.exe /f ""%1"" %*"
+HKCR,Msi.Package\shell\Uninstall\command,,,"%11%\msiexec.exe /x ""%1"" %*"
 HKCR,Msi.Patch,,2,"Windows Installer Patch"
 HKCR,Msi.Patch\DefaultIcon,,2,"msiexec.exe"
 HKCR,Msi.Patch\shell\Open\command,,2,"%11%\msiexec.exe /p ""%1"""
